# public/_redirects
# Netlify redirect rules — copied to dist/ by Astro at build time.
#
# Astro generates static HTML for every route, so a 404 fallback
# isn't needed the way it would be for a SPA. These rules handle
# edge cases and legacy URL cleanup.
#
# Format: /from  /to  status
# Netlify docs: https://docs.netlify.com/routing/redirects/

# ── ADMIN ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Handled by astro.config.ts trailingSlash: 'always' but belt-and-suspenders.
/admin  /admin/  301

# ── WWW → NON-WWW (or flip this if client prefers www) ───────────────────────
# Uncomment whichever applies. Set the canonical domain in Netlify
# dashboard under Domain settings → Primary domain.
# Only one redirect direction should be active at a time.

# Non-www canonical (most common):
# https://www.yourclientdomain.com/*  https://yourclientdomain.com/:splat  301!

# www canonical (less common):
# https://yourclientdomain.com/*  https://www.yourclientdomain.com/:splat  301!

# ── 404 FALLBACK ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Astro generates a 404.html — Netlify serves it automatically for
# unmatched routes. No explicit rule needed.
